mantle rm353
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_philippa_dripworth
title the coal that walks
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=fisher
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=restless
quirk walks_out_a_storm_with_one_lucky_coal_in_each_pocket
likes spiced_cider long_walks old_maps thunder
dislikes haggling early_bells
fears a_quarrel_that_stops_the_winter_fish
hopes a_map_with_a_walk_still_left_on_it
topics travel +0.6 work +0.5 weather +0.4 prices +0.3
styles comfort=direct gossip=exact refuse=firm tease=none
marks oath saying
persona persona #self.first# balances a lucky coal on each hip and would sooner walk the length of a storm than sell a fish under a false description.

words
oath! = Split my thunder coal | Blacken the map border
saying! = A long walk won't freshen a bad fish | Coal travels cheaply in a determined pocket
chip = a thumb-smoothed coal | a split black chip
pouch = my left pocket | the little hip pouch
chart = a map stained at the corners | a worn coastal map
fold = a hill fold | a double-backed road
thunder = a roof-shaking roll | a hollow drum overhead
cider = a spicy apple draught | a steaming cider cup
pan = the low pan | the counter scale
hook = a short steel hook | a carrying hook
board = a scrubbed cutting board | a white fish board
rag = a thick fish rag | a folded salt cloth
belly = a pale belly cut | a fine belly strip
head = the meaty head | a head for broth
tail = a narrow tail cut | a tapered tail
shine = a blue-silver shine | a glaze of silver
cap = a lid of wicker | a split-cane lid
route = the high dry route | the ridge way
slope = the long slope | a mild descent
trunk = a lidded fish chest | a shallow chest
brine = a wash of brine | a pinch of coarse salt

any
opinion merchants mixed 2 : A price written in chalk amounts to a promise. Fish may decline in the course of a day. The truth about them mustn't.
opinion houses against 2 : Come winter we shall need all the landings. I wouldn't have one closed merely to improve somebody's argument.
opinion watch mixed 1 : Look in my basket with clean paws and a stated reason. I can go on serving quite civilly.
opinion dole for 2 : A fish head makes a much better bowl of broth than it makes a performance of charity.
opinion church mixed 1 : Quiet followed by a useful kindness suit my idea of a decent service.
opinion strangers for 1 : Strangers have walked the parts of my map my own legs haven't tested.
opinion festivals mixed 1 : I enjoy a festival walk once the persuasive selling is finished.
opinion road for 2 : I stand by a stretch of ground that gives my restlessness somewhere solid to go.
opinion times against 2 [world.times=lean|hard] : The smaller portions sell first these days, and I'm hearing less talk of next week's supper.

grown
line greet : I'll put my basket down a moment. Welcome. | Take a place on the walking side.
line greet.return : My greeting's got good legs on it too. | Glad we were standing within reach of that welcome.
line again.open : You've come round faster than my boots.
line farewell : Go on sound feet with a little dry space in reserve. | Find a good long stretch without having to bargain for it.
line farewell.return : Your own path be clear to the last stone. | I'll carry that good wish in the clean pocket.
line react.news : Give me the news with its head and tail both on. | I'll hear the account without filleting it first.
line react.news.new : Something new for my route home.
line react.news.known : I know the ground that account covers.
line react.news.doubt : That tale smells older than the date on the wrapping.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : I'd leave supper on the sill for the hurting wolf to find in peace.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : A bright bit worth walking round to share.
line ask.how : How heavy's the road been under you?
line answer.how : Feet itching some, arms steady.
line sympathise : Sit for a minute. I've carried worse than a silence.
line reassure : There's another turning when the rest looks too straight and hard.
line refuse : I promised my two feet to an earlier errand.
line accept_decline : All right. No bargaining over an honest answer.
line preclose : My road's been waiting quite a stretch already.
line accept_preclose : Go claim the rest of the daylight for your feet.
line ack : I reckon I've measured it down to the last inch.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Welcome before the Works have finished rubbing sleep from their eyes.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : A clean board for a newcomer. Step near enough to speak easily.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends] : There's an elbow's width saved for a voice I know.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Come round to the dry corner beside me!
line thank : That'll be a kindness to take along a good long road.
line deflect_thanks : It cost less strength than a carry up the hill.
line give.advice : Ask for the lean side and inspect the fat side as well.
line answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I'm weighing with one eye and keeping the way clear with the other.
line ask.how [pair.band=friends] : Anything setting your feet itching as mine do?
line greet [here.time=night] : There's still a patch of lamplight for the two of us.

scene exchange1
when topic=work self.job=fisher
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I show the gill when a buyer asks about freshness. | I keep the wet cloth off the display.
b : Why not say it's fine? | Shouldn't fish stay damp?
a : An open gill gives a customer something besides my word. | I mean the one I use for my fingers. I keep the two sorts straight.

scene exchange2
when topic=travel self.likes=long_walks
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put a coal in each pocket on a walk. | I can carry a question clear round the hill.
b : Balance the weight? | Does it get answered?
a : Balance the luck. Weight's a very small matter. | It gets rid of every word I didn't need to ask.

scene exchange3
when topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A map gets my thumb on the roads that vanish. | I can walk to a crooked ink line all afternoon.
b : To follow the old way? | Then what?
a : To find exactly where the ground decided otherwise. | Look for the old hedge still following it.

scene exchange4
when topic=weather self.likes=thunder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Thunder moves the coals against my hips. | I prefer thunder with a long tail.
b : Is the ground really shaking? | Can you tell the storm's going?
a : I start walking when I hear it. Same result. | It's easier to hear how far the last bit travelled.

scene exchange5
when topic=food self.likes=spiced_cider
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put both pockets clear before I drink cider. | A good cup leaves the spice till after the apple.
b : What's in them? | And a poor cup?
a : Coal. Luck goes poorly in a hot mug. | Makes a great show of heat to hide a thin beginning.

scene exchange6
when topic=day self.dislikes=early_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Early bells put my feet to work ahead of my head. | An early bell doesn't ask whether my head was up late.
b : Do you manage to ignore the racket? | Do you hold it against the bell?
a : No. I argue with them from the pillow instead. | I hide my ears beneath the blanket.

scene exchange7
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Try the weight before you try the price. | I dislike pricing fish by the customer's patience.
b : And if I can't afford it? | Do you ever bargain?
a : Say that. I'll cut a portion to meet what you've got. | I'd rather offer a smaller piece and keep my arithmetic honest.

scene exchange8
when topic=home self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I save a stretch of my best walk for #self.spouse#. | I've a little piece of coal I'd lend #self.spouse#.
b : How can you save a walk? | Only lend?
a : Leave a fine turning until I've company for it. | I like keeping promises about a return. It means there's another meeting coming.

scene exchange9
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't ask a blessing to make fish out of water. | My lucky coal leaves black on the fingers I fold in prayer.
b : What do you ask? | Does it trouble you?
a : Sense enough to spend the hours when fish are there. | A little clean water sorts out which is coal and which is worry.

scene exchange10
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's what came to the board. | A rumour grows a fine shiny new skin as it travels.
b : Did you see it land? | Will you sell it?
a : The words, yes. Anything else I'd be guessing. | I sell what I can open to inspection.

scene exchange11
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : These lean days I cut smaller pieces earlier. | The head pot sees a lot of custom in hard weeks.
b : Less fish to sell? | Is the broth good?
a : Less certainty about whose purse can take a large parcel. | I make sure a wolf coming for economy gets flavour thrown in.

scene exchange12
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I fear the Houses may fall into quarrelling before winter. | I'd prize a map whose margin outspans the drawn country.
b : Has a dispute begun? | What would you add?
a : It's my fear, not market news. I want the landings kept open. | A record of the places I haven't thought to walk to yet.

scene exchange13
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The Sump to the Heights makes a good long measure for a day. | Over the basket rims I read black smoke rising from the Works.
b : Do you climb for custom? | Is it a weather sign?
a : For the view of all the streets I've just passed through. | A reminder which way down is homeward.

scene exchange14
when topic=work self.role=merchant self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I display the small offcuts as plainly as the best fillets. | I face my scale towards the open side.
b : To tempt a cook? | For the light?
a : To spare a hungry buyer asking what the cheap end costs. | For the eyes over the counter. My eyes already know my trade.

scene exchange15
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A long tramp eases a shoulder that has spent all day over scales. | I take the light basket when I've a stitch in my side.
b : Doesn't it tire your feet? | A very small load?
a : I give the worries to a different pair of joints. | An empty basket. I can respect an honest warning.

scene exchange16
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Turning the pockets out is my last chore. | I put one coal away before I sweep the other up.
b : Do you set the coals in the hearth? | Why the order?
a : My walking coals have earned their own dry saucer. | The good luck shouldn't go out with the sweepings.

scene exchange17
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A late wagon can't be cut into tonight's portions. | If a load's late I leave the chalk down.
b : Do customers keep asking? | No prices at all?
a : I tell them what actually arrived, then show my board. | None for goods I can't yet weigh.

scene exchange18
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A fish tail cooks quicker than the shoulder. | I leave the skin across the tender white flesh.
b : How do you arrange supper? | Why let it hide?
a : Thick piece in first. Company can wait together at the plate. | In the pan, for protection. I'll show a buyer both sides beforehand.

scene exchange19
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I ask a stranger how far supper has to travel. | I point out the slope with the basket hand empty.
b : A nosy question? | Why change hands?
a : A wrapper for two doors differs from one for two hills. | So a visitor sees the actual turn and not a parcel waving in the wind.

scene exchange20
when topic=work self.job=fisher
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A fish bone has a different slant on each side of the backbone. | I can test a blade on the scrap at the edge.
b : How do you find it? | Safer than your thumb?
a : Let the blade follow instead of forcing it straight. | A great deal less personal if the result's poor.

scene exchange21
when topic=prices self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I set the wrapped weight and the bare weight apart. | The cheapest piece may take the longest cooking.
b : What does the buyer pay? | Do you tell a customer?
a : For the fish. Paper's a convenience, not a surprise portion. | A fair price ought to reckon fuel too.

scene exchange22
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My first lucky chip had a bright little stripe in it. | I used to keep my coal loose with the coppers.
b : Is there still a stripe? | Did you pay with luck?
a : Smoothed clear off. I know the chip by the gap it left. | Nearly. I started giving the two different lodgings.

scene exchange23
when topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My old map sends a street straight into water. | I trace an unknown turn with a washed claw tip.
b : Old ferry crossing? | Why not use coal?
a : Or merely an optimist with a pen. I'll walk out and see. | Old ink deserves leaving as I found it.

scene exchange24
when topic=weather self.likes=thunder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a count to keep after lightning and before its roar. | A storm coming off the Sound has a broad voice.
b : To work out the distance? | Does it drown out the sellers?
a : To see if this time I have leisure to get my cloth down. | For once even the most persuasive buyer goes quiet.

scene exchange25
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The hook for my map is above the one for my market coat. | I turn the pocket seam outward over a basin.
b : Have many maps washed out? | Catching last week's luck?
a : One was an excellent education. | Coal grit. I don't want it seasoning supper.

scene exchange26
when topic=work self.job=fisher
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I trim a cut so it can sit flat. | Salt belongs on the fish the buyer intends to salt.
b : In the scale pan? | What about drying it?
a : In the frying pan. That's where the sale finishes. | First I make sure it's meant to keep, rather than go straight to supper.

scene exchange27
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd spare #self.friend# the salesman part of my voice. | I go a little slower with a friend who stops to look at things.
b : What part is left? | Do you begrudge the time?
a : The bit that likes a long walk in company. | No. A longer walk is generally what I wanted.

scene exchange28
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Winter boards have less give beneath a foot. | A colder morning makes a clean scale seem almost sharp.
b : Do you walk differently? | Does that slow the weighing?
a : I keep the stride shorter and the head up for what's ahead. | Speed comes second to finding my fingers unhurt.

scene exchange29
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember my first proper long walk by the spice I smelled on returning. | I went looking for a lane which used to turn towards a kiln.
b : A homecoming cup? | Was the kiln gone?
a : A stranger's open shutter. It counted all the same. | Long gone, but the road still bowed politely to its old doorstep.

scene exchange30
when topic=travel self.likes=long_walks
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't always retrace an outward walk. | I find an odd coin in a walk's old pocket sometimes.
b : Afraid of wearing a groove? | Would you wish for more?
a : Interested in the other sides of the same houses. | Enough for hot cider. Too much in a pocket gives the coat an inconvenient list.

story tale1 [topic=work self.job=fisher]
  : I once set two lovely fish tails out with their tips almost touching. I made a serious effort to keep the arrangement neat as little orders went by.
  : Late in the day a buyer asked for the bit in the middle. It was an almost invisible piece of empty board.
  b : What did you put in the parcel?
  : A decent middle cut from under the cloth. I let the tails go back to the useful work of becoming suppers.

story tale2 [topic=travel]
  : My old pocket wore through where the coal sat, dropped into the lining and made the coat hang crooked for a week.
  : When I shook it free an old copper fell out too.
  b : Did you thank the coal?
  : I spent the copper on spice and mended the lining. The coal still travels with me.

story tale3 [topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps]
  : I found a road drawn twice on an old map, a fine straight route with another waving gently alongside. I took the straight one out.
  : The way actually curved round every little hillock. The straight line was the edge of an ancient fold.
  b : Did you mark the mistake?
  : I marked my own route on separate paper. The map had never promised to be flat.

story tale4 [topic=weather self.likes=thunder]
  : One full roll of thunder sent the spoons in my drying rack rattling from left to right. I lined them up by size for the next roll.
  : The smallest one gave a little flick and sent its neighbour off the end.
  b : Where did the spoon land?
  : In my boot. A dry thunderstorm had found a truly remarkable way of interrupting my walk.

story tale5 [topic=food self.likes=spiced_cider]
  : I carried a small cup of warm cider up a long slope to save it for a better view. I turned at the summit with all the ceremony of a grand toast.
  : The steam had risen away and the spice had settled to the bottom.
  b : Did the view improve the cup?
  : I stirred with a clean twig end and drank. Next time I'll bring the cup to my mouth while I'm still looking forward to the view.

rule @call1
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=fisher
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Bright and firm across this cut. | Take a look beneath the shiny skin.

rule @call2
when concept=bark working=yes self.role=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Price plain enough for a wet morning. | No extra for the outside of the parcel.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Tuck the old map round the dry side. | Rain can have the coat and leave my coals alone.

rule @call4
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Bells have borrowed a good half of my dream. | Feet first, ears can catch up.

rule @call5
when concept=bark self.likes=long_walks
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A long stretch would shake this restlessness out. | My boots have another hill's worth left.

rule @call6
when concept=bark self.likes=spiced_cider
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Something hot with a spice twist would do just now. | A warm mug beats a noisy bargain.
dlg resident.hub : I've walked the impatience out of myself for the moment. Speak freely.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, there's nobody between you and a straight answer here.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : I can spare a bit of the late walk for talking.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Watch my hands, watch the board. I keep the words just as plain.
dlg resident.job [self.job=fisher] : I know what's been cut, what's been salted and what belongs in a pot. My trade's right here on the board.
dlg resident.job : I want both of us clear about what changed hands when a deal's done.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The news has travelled this length of street. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. A report isn't the same as a fish in my paw.
dlg resident.bye : May you get both a dry route and a bit of weather to look at.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=open] : Look underneath any cut before you choose. I've chalked the honest price in an easy spot to see.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : Nothing to wrap just now. There's no sense weighing the bare board.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=asleep] : Even the fish boards are shut. Come on a waking visit.
dlg shop.prices : The figure you see belongs to the fish you see. Inspect before you pay.
dlg shop.bye [here.shop!=asleep] : Keep the thick side of the parcel underneath.
dlg resident.business [business=failing] : Too many fine-looking fish and too few suppers calling for them.
dlg resident.business [business=steady] : The usual customers keep my pots washed and my board moving.
dlg resident.business [business=thriving] : There's a warm pot waiting for almost every piece before I finish wrapping it.

graft resident.hub
choice Why carry two pieces of coal? -> walk_coals
node walk_coals
say One goes on every journey. Its partner wants an equally grand journey. I turn for home when my feet begin to feel the argument.
free
choice Do you ever lend one? -> walk_coals_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node walk_coals_again
say If somebody has a longer way ahead than I do. A private bit of luck can manage a night away.
choice Keep the lining mended. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice Can this cut stand a long walk? [here.shop=open] -> fish_way
node fish_way
say I can wrap it for a journey, but distance isn't the only thing that counts. Tell me how soon the pan will get hot.
free
choice Why ask about the pan? -> fish_way_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node fish_way_again
say I'd sooner sell something that keeps properly than promise a fresh supper that can't arrive so. I'll explain any difference in price first.
choice I'll look at the other cuts. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye
